# Target C: zero-state closure certificates for finite owner moves

Date: 2026-10-05. Base main: `0351c2c3aecd34c0427d0ad081afae563468d401`.
State: `2026-10-05.audit.61`.
Classification: **proved candidate synthesis awaiting independent audit**;
artifact lifecycle **unreviewed**. This uses elementary Horn closure;
no novelty is claimed for the Boolean theorem. C-II and Level I remain open.

## 1. Exact implication

```
canonical finite disjoint-owner move and a pinned shortening state
-> its all-zero-valid pair formula has implication/negative-clause form
-> close the pinned-true owners under directed implications
-> either explicit admissible shortening assignment, or a path to a
   forbidden owner / two paths to a forbidden simultaneous pair
-> source-level failure has a directed path or fork certificate,
   not merely an owner cycle.
```

The only canonical Boolean input is C-DISJOINT-SWAP-2SAT, Sections 1--4
of the promoted simultaneous-swap report and audit.60's Section 4.
For actual sufficiently small O--O motions, audit.61 additionally
localizes the lower clauses to outer-face pairs and unary rhombus tests.
Neither input supplies a move family or excludes every failure certificate.

## 2. The exact zero-state form

In canonical finite compilation, the all-zero assignment is the original
source and is admissible. Thus no source pair can forbid local state 00.
After omitting tautologies and repeated clauses, every clause is one of

    x_i -> x_j,
    not(x_i and x_j),
    not x_i.

The first forbids 10 or, with reversed labels, 01. The second forbids 11.
A unary clause can only forbid 1. Distinct-owner clauses have i!=j;
a repeated-variable negative clause is folded into the unary list.
There is no positive-positive clause demanding selection of an owner.
This form holds for arbitrary prescribed translations satisfying the
canonical disjoint-owner/contact-preservation hypotheses; equal
translations are not needed.

Write Q for the directed implication graph, Z for the unary-forbidden
owners, and F for the unordered forbidden simultaneous pairs. For pinned
true owners P and pinned false owners N, let C(P) be the forward reachable
closure of P in Q, including P.

## 3. Pinned closure theorem

The pinned formula has a model exactly when

    C(P) intersects (Z union N) trivially,
    no pair in F has both endpoints in C(P).           (3.1)

When (3.1) holds, setting exactly C(P) true and all other owners false is
an explicit model.

**Proof.** Every model containing P contains its reachable closure, so
both conditions are necessary. Conversely that closure is closed under
every implication. Its complement can be false: negative clauses impose
no requirement to add further true owners. The two conditions enforce
all unary and pair exclusions, and the pins are respected. QED.

A failed pin therefore has one of two concrete certificates:

1. a directed path from a member of P to Z or N;
2. a forbidden pair uv, and directed paths from members of P to u and v.

Paths can be chosen simple, each of length at most k-1. The two origins
can coincide, producing a fork, or differ for a two-owner pinned state.
Cycles can occur in Q but are not necessary in either certificate.

Each locally shortening diameter state has at least one pinned true
owner because state 00 is unchanged. It has at most two pinned owners,
with a possible false pin in state 10 or 01. Thus (3.1) decides every
canonical pinned shortening test exactly. If it passes, the explicitly
constructed closure assignment is a full-source competitor by the
canonical 2-SAT compilation and normalization consequence.

## 4. Sink classes and what cycles do not prove

Contract the directed strongly connected components of Q. The unpinned
formula has a nonzero model exactly when at least one sink component S
has

    S intersects Z trivially,
    no pair in F lies entirely in S.                 (4.1)

**Proof.** Such a sink is implication-closed, so its indicator is a
model. Conversely any nonempty true set is closed and contains a global
sink component reachable from any one of its true components. That sink
cannot contain a unary prohibition or an internal forbidden pair. QED.

A directed implication cycle by itself is harmless: a three-owner cycle
has models 000 and 111. A cycle of pure simultaneous conflicts is also
harmless for singleton selection: a conflict triangle has models 000,
100,010,001. By contrast the acyclic implications 1->2 and 1->3 together
with the forbidden pair 23 block the pin x_1=1. Hence cycle elimination
alone is neither necessary nor sufficient for a proposed beneficial pin.
These are abstract Boolean certificates, not canonical source examples.

If Q is acyclic and Z is empty, there is a singleton sink, so there is
a nonzero model regardless of F. Turning that fact into a diameter
contradiction requires proving that this model shortens an old diameter.
Neutral repair owners can be sinks; they cannot be silently counted as
beneficial. In general one must test the actual locally shortening
patterns through Section 3.

## 5. Composition with audit.61 geometry

For an actual small stopped O--O motion satisfying the promoted cloud,
ownership, isolate-dispatch and rhombus hypotheses, every lower clause
in the preceding certificates is supported on an actual outer-face pair,
except the explicit unary rhombus tests. Inactive upper exceptions remain
in the separately bounded set; old diameter constraints remain explicit.
If all upper constraints and unary rhombi have been certified harmless,
the remaining failure is an outer-face directed path to a fixed/forbidden
owner or an outer-face conflict pair reached by two propagation paths.

This is the exact next geometric target. A source matching becoming an
owner cycle is not by itself a failed shortening certificate. The binding
owner-contraction regression is respected: source-path acyclicity does
not imply owner acyclicity, and neither is assumed here. Actual ownership
may identify distant source vertices, so a directed owner path is not
asserted to be a contiguous source path or a boundary interval.

No promoted return quota, midpoint bound or residual-cage coordinate
claim cited here excludes all these outer-face path/fork certificates.
No full-core or container branch is closed. The repeated two-phase
specialization in Section 5 of the older swap report is unpromoted and
is not used as a premise.

## 6. Exact verifier

Run `python3 research/verify_target_c_zero_state_horn_closure_2026_10_05.py`.
It exhaustively checks all 4,131 formulas generated from all possible
zero-valid nontrivial unary, implication and negative-pair clauses on
zero through three variables. It compares 110,887 pinned closure tests
against full truth-table enumeration and checks the sink criterion for
every formula. It also certifies the harmless directed cycle, harmless
pure-conflict cycle and acyclic blocking fork.

The verifier proves finite Boolean identities only. It does not encode
source coordinates, contact preservation, O--O extraction, beneficial
states, loaded-return geometry, KKT or global optimality. The general
proofs above are analytic. Repository checks validate lifecycle/index
consistency, not C-II closure.
